WEBVTT

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.230
<b>May 24th   12:00 AM   Hakata</b>

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.300
Oh, yeah?

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.360
Here you go!

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.820
Want to check out a lingerie club?

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.780
Come again!

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:26.790
Then the bastard just...

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.970
<b>Banba Private Investigations</b>

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.850
So... who're you?

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.240
A hitman.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.360
Someone hired me to kill you.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.950
<b>18 Hours Ago   6:00 AM</b>

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.610
Who is it so early in the morning?

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.370
Takashi's here, isn't he?

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.850
Let me see him.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.040
He's been cheating on me.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:07.720
Cheating?

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.200
As if he'd be serious about a woman like y—

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.490
I'm not trying to take him back.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.840
I'm just here to shove the bag 
he got for me in his face.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.170
It'd be nice if I could punch him one, too.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.010
Then sure, I guess.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.460
Just make it quick.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.360
Hey, Akemi, is someone—

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.620
I hate having women as targets.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.620
Wh-Who the hell are you?!

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.080
Me? A hitman.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.400
Y-You coward!

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.060
You even dressed up as a woman!

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:52.340
Idiot. This is just a hobby.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.710
I like cross-dressing.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.550
You know about the organization behind 
the club called Miroir, right?

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.020
You know what'll happen if you run off 
with something that isn't yours, right?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.720
They can have the money!

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.430
I still have four million!

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.430
That's less than half.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:12.680
Besides, they don't want the money back.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.180
They just want to make an example out of you.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.140
Then I'll give you the money! So—

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.810
Let you run?

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.010
Well, I owe some money, too.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:25.330
That's not a bad offer...

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.580
But, you know...

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.060
Once I accept a job, I have to follow through.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.350
I'm a professional, after all.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.740
<b>#01 Play Ball</b>

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.900
I never get tired of that sound.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.240
She's cute!

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.230
Idiot. I'm a guy.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.670
<b>Zhang
Incoming Call</b>

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.670
Man, Zhang?

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.380
Hello?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.740
If it's about the couple who 
made off with the money—

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.690
Huh? Another one?

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.630
I just finished the job I had.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.300
A detective?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.130
That's a different story, then.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:26.850
Any blueblood costs double, you know.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.470
I know.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.410
Just send me the address already.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:35.290
<i>I can be done with this piece of shit soon.</i>

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.630
<i>Once I pay back the money I owe...</i>

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.370
<i>Qiaomei.</i>

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.570
Brother!

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.430
Brother!

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.730
I'm almost done.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.770
Hang in there, Qiaomei.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:15.020
<b>Shinjuku    Tokyo</b>

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.480
Red Rum, Inc.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.480
Huh? Weren't you starting at 
the Fukuoka branch today?

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.060
Er, yes.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:21.990
I'm about to catch the bullet train there.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.950
I just forgot something.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.570
Some memorable baseball 
that won a game or something?

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:31.290
I'd say it's more accurate to call 
it unforgettable than memorable.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.190
We only got to work together 
for two months or so,

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.340
but thanks for everything, Gwen-san!

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.950
Nah, you don't owe me a thing.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.010
Good luck over there, Saito-kun.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.850
I sure need it.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.520
I hear three percent of the population 
there is in our line of work.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.970
I hope a wimp can me can compete.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.140
That's it?!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.100
I said I want something meatier!

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.940
I'm bored to death with all 
these jobs I can do half asleep!

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.700
People like him are much more 
suited for this line of work.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.430
He's in a class of his own.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.510
Well, I'll get going.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:08.320
All right.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:15.750
Well, it's true that this job 
isn't a good fit for you.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.210
Gotta wonder why you joined this company...

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.090
A company of killers for hire.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.630
<b>Fukuoka City   Higashi Ward</b>

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.620
This is the place, right?

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.560
I heard he hung himself.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.700
Was he really lonely?

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.630
His wife left him, right?

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:38.270
Maybe it was job stress.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.680
Takeda-san was a detective, I think.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:41.450
Huh?

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.260
Suicide...

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:49.620
I didn't do the job, but dead is dead.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:53.850
It's me.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.640
The detective's dead, too.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:00.170
There are small bruises in addition 
to the marks left by the rope.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:04.000
Marks left precisely on the 
throat, artery, and vein...

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.600
It was strangulation made 
to look like a suicide.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.260
You think so too, huh?

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.960
Yeah, it was a professional job.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:12.730
Who's the target?

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:17.270
A detective named Takeda who was in charge 
of dealing with gangs at my precinct.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.530
His body was found this morning.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.710
According to his suicide note,

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:29.350
he offed himself because he was about 
to be discovered taking evidence.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:33.250
But you aren't convinced, 
are you, Shigematsu-san?

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:36.230
He looked out for me when I was younger.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:39.800
Sometimes, even when you try to throw a 
forkball, it becomes a four-seam fastball.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:44.230
That's the kind of man he was.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:51.990
This was delivered to my place yesterday.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:56.720
There was no sender, but it 
had to have been Takeda-san.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:00.890
So he had an inkling that 
he was about to get offed...

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:01.730
Huh?

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:03.690
This is...

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:04.840
Yeah.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:09.570
Hakata's economy and safety have 
improved over the past four years.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.570
<b>Harada Shotaro</b>

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.780
But we're only halfway there.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:17.660
Please give me, Harada Shotaro, 
another four years to improve Hakata!

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.150
It's the mayor.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.670
The babe's with him, too.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:28.900
Please lend me your support in 
the upcoming mayoral election!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.300
<b>Please 
Give
Your
Vote!</b>

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.020
What are you doing?

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.170
Just seeing how the broad would react.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:00.750
A fake gunshot, huh?

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:03.160
If she freezes, she's just a secretary.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.880
If she tries to shield him, she's a bodyguard.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.750
So what's the verdict?

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.250
That was a hitman's reaction.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:15.340
But I don't think she was 
responsible for Takeda-san.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.310
She has long, pretty nails.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.650
You've got a good eye.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:24.860
So, Banba, about that favor I wanted to ask...

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:26.060
No problem.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.360
Whatever Mayor Harada is up to,

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.860
he's dirty enough to hire a hitman.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:36.200
Let's air out the dirty laundry.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.930
Good work today, Reiko-san.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:48.610
Anything of note?

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:49.960
There was a gunshot.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:55.080
Or so I thought, but it was just 
some idiot popping a balloon.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:56.430
What about your end?

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.980
Ivanov got the deed done.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.520
The detective's death 
will be deemed a suicide.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:06.360
And I made sure he'll be discredited 
as a dirty cop who took evidence.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:10.160
Was all that necessary?

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:11.260
Who knows?

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.660
We had no choice.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.170
Public servants have to do as they're told

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.330
by whoever's highest on the food chain.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.080
Speak of the devil...

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:23.400
Hello?

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.810
<i>Munakata-san, it's me again.</i>

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:28.830
That damn idiot son.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.850
Sorry, I messed up again.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:34.360
Can you clean up after me?

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.090
Oh, thanks.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.280
It's fine. There's no rush.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.050
Thanks a bunch!

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:52.190
<i>So this is the city where three percent 
of the population's said to be hitmen...</i>

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:52.650
<b>Hakata</b>

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.110
<b>Hakata</b>

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:53.570
<b>Hakata</b>

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:54.280
<b>Hakata</b>

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.030
<i>Hakata!</i>

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:59.130
<i>Come on, me! Get it together!</i>

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.500
<i>So where's the 100-yen bus?</i>

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:10.790
Man, you're really sticking 
your neck out again, Banba-san.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:14.500
Well, this case has already caused one death.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.640
Wow, really?

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:17.720
Sounds dangerous.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.310
Well, how's it looking, Enokida-kun?

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:21.300
Think you can do it?

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:24.870
You think there's anything I can't handle?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.310
I could even turn all the traffic
lights in the city red, you know.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.130
Want me to do it now?

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:31.310
I'm done with this, anyway.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.520
Oh, already?

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.610
See? Here it is.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.100
Asakura Reiko.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.280
Worked at Red Rum, Inc. until five years ago.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.500
Red Rum? That's...

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:43.990
Yup.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:47.220
Red Rum, Inc.

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:48.260
Everyone in our line of work knows Red Rum.

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:50.920
A company of killers for hire: Murder, Inc.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:55.920
Just as you suspected, she's a hitman.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.170
A former club hostess from Nakasu,

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.630
she specializes in using poison.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:04.930
I bet she cozies up to VIPs 
and kills them slowly

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.730
by slipping poison into their drinks.

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:09.350
Scary business.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.780
There's no further information 
available on her.

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:16.020
So she must've been working for 
the mayor for the past five years.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:18.360
Maybe she was hand-picked for the job.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:23.000
Female hitmen are pretty useful if 
they're outwardly acting as secretaries.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:27.110
Are there any other former Murder, Inc. 
employees that quit around that time

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:29.330
who like to kill by strangulation?

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.810
Strangulation?

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.040
Oh, yeah, there's one.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:35.320
Ivanov Hisashi.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:37.480
Half Japanese, half Russian.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:40.920
Specializes in both ligature 
and manual strangulation.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.960
So, who's this girl?

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.430
No idea.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.510
Just some girl off the streets.

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:51.730
She made a fuss when I tried 
to bang her, so I killed her.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.040
I don't understand.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:54.930
Ivanov.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.770
Shino, hold that end.

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:02.150
Manual labor isn't part 
of my job description.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:12.540
Hey, did you know killing people is illegal?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.960
Oh, nice joke.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.370
I don't dislike jokes like that 
at all, killer Reiko-san.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:24.140
Listen, it's not like I want
to cause you trouble.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:25.610
But I can't help it.

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:27.860
I just get the urge sometimes.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:29.770
Look, you...

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.820
Don't get mad at me.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.920
I gave proper notice this time, didn't I?

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.300
Well, of course.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.610
We can't have you ditching bodies 
in random places all the time.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.870
How much work do you think 
it takes to cover up—

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.570
My apologies.

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:47.030
This causes your father problems, too.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:48.490
Do you get that?

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:52.500
Who cares about someone like him?

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:55.370
Anyway, thanks for your help going forward.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.440
<i>Stop!</i>

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.340
<i>Please!</i>

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.200
<i>Keep it up, Murase!</i>

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:00.200
<i>Please!</i>

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:01.050
<i>Damn!</i>

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:02.110
<i>He knows what we look like, right?</i>

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:02.970
What's that?

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:03.880
Oh, this?

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:07.530
It's a video of my club members 
attacking some foreigner

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.640
because I told them to in the King's Game.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.110
Isn't it fun?

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:15.030
I was thinking of uploading it to the net.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.390
No uploads.

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:25.030
Give us the names of all the friends of
yours who was there when it happened.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:31.740
Munakata-san, we have another problem.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:37.420
I was walking with a friend.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.880
Then we were suddenly attacked!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.340
I ran, but they caught my friend...

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.280
It's okay.

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.300
You don't have to force yourself to talk.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.950
He got lynched by three people.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:52.890
He's now in a coma in critical condition.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.320
Cruel, I tell you...

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:59.560
My friend was holding this.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.020
It probably belongs to one of them...

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:04.110
<b>Murase Jun</b>

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.110
Murase Jun?

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.200
And what do you want us to do?

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.570
Revenge!

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.580
Well, the avenger has accepted the job.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.580
Murase Jun 

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.670
Murase Jun... A college student?

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.300
The client's one of his neighbors.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:27.300
He's always causing a racket 
and being a nuisance.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.880
Can you get rid of him?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.340
Yes, sir!

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:34.240
Good, good. You're bright-eyed 
and bushy-tailed.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.980
Oh, here.

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.430
Business cards for your cover.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.150
Fukuoka Branch 
Sales Division

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.150
Red Rum, Inc.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:40.150
From today on, you're Ito Takuya-kun!

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.930
Thank you.

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:42.790
I'll be off, then.

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:43.730
Oh, hang on.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:46.910
If you're going to be a hitman in Hakata,

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.210
be careful of the hitmen hitman.

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:51.780
The hitmen hitman?

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:54.910
A hitman specializing 
in killing other hitmen.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.120
He calls himself the opportunistic samurai.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.540
The opportunistic samurai...

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.810
But I think you'll be safe enough.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:05.590
Only hitmen worth their salt 
would be targeted, after all.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.800
Right.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:14.310
The mayor, a hitman, and Miroir.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:19.430
My wallet.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:22.010
I'd like to have it back, Yamato-kun.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.240
Oh, you knew?

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:28.440
So, what'd you want to ask me about?

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:30.820
Is it about this?

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:35.280
<b>Gen-chan
Oden</b>

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.280
Well, I don't know this bloke.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:39.270
But this one works at a club called Miroir.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:40.500
Miroir...

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.210
He was killed this morning.

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:44.880
Along with his girlfriend.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:45.660
Huh?

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.210
Genzou-san, another serving 
of noodles, extra firm.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.200
Coming right up.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:50.330
Why?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.180
What? Got something against 
extra firm noodles?

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:55.220
Not that. Why was he killed?

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:58.570
Oh, he skimmed ten million 
off the club's profits,

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:01.250
so the club hired a hitman.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.710
They have a pretty shady backer or something.

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.150
Here you go. Extra firm.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.170
Thanks.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.930
This must've been for that club worker.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:22.080
Then this one's...

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.540
Thanks for the ramen!

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:31.460
The plot keeps getting thicker.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:34.680
I wonder if Enokida-kun's hearing all this.

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:36.230
Hey!

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.440
What's that?

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:40.390
I got it from Enokida-kun.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:45.600
It's a GPS-equipped "redback spider" model bug.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:49.770
That trickster's making more 
of his odd contraptions again.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:53.890
I wonder why the spider's 
got a red back, though.

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:54.450
Huh?

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:58.190
A normal black spider'd just blend right in.

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:02.790
This is like screaming, "I'm a 
venomous spider!" Don't you think?

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:05.530
You've got to be kidding me!

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:07.800
Only 3,000 yen? Are you messing with me?!

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:10.090
I'm not the one who screwed up!

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.090
Hey, are you listening to me?!

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:13.900
We can't resolve this by phone.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.930
I'm coming over right now, you hear?!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:16.850
Damn it!

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:21.310
Hey, you.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:23.350
What?

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:26.600
You touched my ass just now, didn't you?

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:31.570
I'm in a really bad mood today!

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:31.570
Hey, wait!

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:34.650
Die, perv.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:39.210
You'll pay for this, shemale!

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:40.950
I mean he-female!

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.330
I'm gonna make him pay...

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:47.040
Thank you for coming!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:53.210
<b>Natural Twine</b>

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:53.210
<b>Packing Tape</b>

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:53.210
<b>Rubber Gloves</b>

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:52.500
<i>Can I really kill someone?</i>

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.130
"Newcomers to baseball welcome"?

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.720
<b>Desperately Need Pitcher 
and Shortstop!</b>

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.720
<b>Baseball Club Members Wanted!</b>

00:17:58.620 --> 00:18:00.720
Looking for a pitcher and a shortstop?

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:04.690
For some people, this would be enough 
to get them into baseball...

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:08.310
Right. I can be that way, too!

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:12.610
You're a detective?

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:15.530
The mayor's been here, right?

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.950
I want to ask some questions about 
the person who came here with him.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.030
Well, I don't remember anything.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:23.720
I see.

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.040
Thanks anyway.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.500
Come on, get it together.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.960
Get it together...

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.650
Can I do this?

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.600
He's back!

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:37.860
But why would Murase ring his own doorbell?

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.770
A dad and kid?

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:48.760
Yes?

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:50.520
Oh, hello.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:53.210
Sorry to bother you so late at night.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:56.090
We just moved in downstairs. I'm Tanaka.

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:58.610
This is a small gift.

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.300
Oh, how thoughtful of you.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.530
I really appreciate—

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:19.080
Man, he's really careless for an adult.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:23.370
Now, let's go on a little trip, Murase Jun-kun.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:31.960
Like I said, that detective job 
basically got cut short on <i>your</i> end!

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.350
At least pay me half!

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:36.760
But did you even have anything 
to do with his death?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.230
You didn't, right?

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:42.700
Maybe he killed himself because he knew 
I was coming for him and got scared.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:45.110
You've got quite the ego, boy.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.680
It wasn't a suicide.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:49.120
He was killed.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.010
Huh?

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:53.910
A different hitman got to him 
first, then strung him up.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.450
You don't even consider things like that.

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:58.940
That's why you'll always be an amateur.

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:00.630
I'm not an amateur!

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:04.510
Right, right. You're a professional hitman.

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:07.320
If you keep running your mouth,

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:09.770
I'll just have the opportunistic 
samurai deal with you.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.970
Heh, right. The hitmen hitman 
everyone's talking about?

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.620
I wonder if he even really exists.

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:16.900
Anyway, I want my money—

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:21.440
If you're that starved for cash, go kill him.

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.780
Banba Private Investigations

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:24.780
He was sniffing around our business.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.940
He's an eyesore.

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:28.740
Get rid of him tonight.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:33.550
I see.

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:35.290
He's quite a handful.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:39.250
Given the frequency, there's no 
telling when someone might find out.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.490
Maybe you need to talk to your son...

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:44.800
It's because he's killing civilians.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.340
Huh?

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:48.790
There's an organization 
dealing in human trafficking.

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:52.230
Buy women who have no family 
from them and let him have them.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:56.940
If there are no missing persons reports, 
it'll be less likely to become a problem.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:20:59.860
Understood.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.120
<b>Banba Private Investigations</b>

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:19.090
What? <i>That's</i> how they hook up?

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:21.840
What the hell? No way.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:25.800
Who're you?

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.710
Are you Baba Zenji?

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:31.060
You do have a horsey face, I guess.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:33.250
It's Banba, not Baba.

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:35.180
And who are you?

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:37.490
A hitman.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:39.690
Someone hired me to kill you.

00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:49.240
What was that for?

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:51.910
Just protecting myself.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.330
You're a hitman, right?

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:57.090
Yeah, I am. A professional.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:59.790
But I'm not here to kill you.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:00.920
Huh?

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:05.640
I thought I'd protect you.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:41.020
#02 Irregular
